@startuml
' purpose: how a def entrypoint tells the agent which verification commands the project supports
' covers: internal/verify/**
' covers: cmd/proveo-entrypoint/**
' covers: defs/*/entrypoint.sh (the verification block)
' covers: defs/claudecode/mcp/entrypoint.sh (the verification block)
' covers: internal/contract/defaults_test.go (TestDeadHostLibsRemoved)
'
' ── ONE IMPLEMENTATION: proveo-entrypoint verify (N4, DONE (wt) 2026-10-17) ─
' The user: "Delete all three (Recommended)" (repo-simplification.puml N4).
' MEASURED: the three identical detect-verify.sh shell wrappers
' (defs/lib/, defs/cecli/proveo-lib/, defs/claudecode/mcp/proveo-lib/) are
' deleted, and so are the now-empty defs/lib/ and defs/cecli/proveo-lib/
' (internal/contract/defaults_test.go TestDeadHostLibsRemoved).
' defs/claudecode/mcp/proveo-lib/ went with the Claude in Chrome bridge
' (2026-10-24). Every def
' entrypoint that prints the block (codex, opencode, cursor, cecli,
' claudecode/mcp) runs it only `if command -v proveo-entrypoint`; the
' `elif … detect-verify` fallbacks and the lib COPY lines (codex, opencode,
' cursor, hermes, cecli) are gone. Every proveo image bakes the binary
' (defs/base/Dockerfile; the floor probe), and imagetest asserts it as
' "proveo-entrypoint (verification commands) is baked" with `command -v
' proveo-entrypoint` (codex_test.go:101, cursor_test.go:90).
' HISTORY: the wrapper kept the name detect-verify.sh so baked /opt/proveo/lib/
' paths worked for images without the Go binary, and it carried a dev fallback
' (`go run ./cmd/proveo-entrypoint verify` from the nearest go.mod). No current
' image lacks the binary, so the fallbacks were unreachable.

!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
title Verification-command discovery — telling the agent how to check its own work

node "Agent container" as CTR <<host>> {
  component "def entrypoint preamble" as SH <<app>>
  component "proveo-entrypoint verify <dir>\n(internal/verify)" as VER <<app>>
  component "Detect(root, lookPath)\n→ []Command{category, command}" as DET <<app>>
  component "FormatLines(cmds)\ncategory|command" as FMT <<app>>
  folder "Mounted workspace" as WS <<db>> {
    artifact "go.mod" as GOMOD <<db>>
    artifact "package.json + lockfile" as PKG <<db>>
    artifact "Cargo.toml" as CARGO <<db>>
    artifact "Dockerfile / compose" as DOCKER <<db>>
  }
  component "agent CLI\nreads the printed block" as AGENT <<app>>
}

SH ARROW_MAIN VER : " ""verify $(pwd)"" "
VER ARROW_MAIN DET
DET ARROW_MAIN WS : detect project shape
GOMOD ARROW_OPTIONAL DET
PKG ARROW_OPTIONAL DET
CARGO ARROW_OPTIONAL DET
DOCKER ARROW_OPTIONAL DET
DET ARROW_MAIN FMT
FMT ARROW_MAIN SH : "── Verification Commands ──"
SH ARROW_MAIN AGENT : preamble on stdout

note right of DET
  **Two gates, both required.** A command is suggested
  only when the project manifest exists **and** the tool
  resolves on PATH (""lookPath""). Suggesting ""cargo test""
  in an image without cargo would send the agent into a
  loop against a missing binary.

  Detection is per-language and additive: a polyglot
  monorepo yields several categories at once.
end note

note bottom of AGENT
  This is advisory context, not enforcement — nothing
  runs these for the agent. It exists so an autonomous
  loop closes with a real check instead of the model
  inventing a build command that does not exist in
  this repo.

  The Go detector is the only one: the shell
  fallbacks were deleted (N4), and an image without
  ""proveo-entrypoint"" simply prints no block.
end note
@enduml
